WEBVTT

00:00:01.919 --> 00:00:05.650
Captain's Log, Stardate 47423.9.

00:00:05.689 --> 00:00:07.554
We have arrived at Boraal II

00:00:07.591 --> 00:00:09.650
in response to an emergency
distress call

00:00:09.693 --> 00:00:12.389
from Lieutenant Worf's foster
brother, Nikolai Rozhenko.

00:00:12.429 --> 00:00:14.056
He has been stationed
on the planet

00:00:14.097 --> 00:00:15.223
as a cultural observer.

00:00:16.566 --> 00:00:18.363
Analysis, Mr. Data.

00:00:18.402 --> 00:00:21.030
The planet's atmosphere
is dissipating, sir.

00:00:21.071 --> 00:00:24.404
Intense plasmonic reactions
are destroying it.

00:00:24.441 --> 00:00:27.001
The stratosphere is
already breaking down.

00:00:27.044 --> 00:00:29.205
There are turbulent
radiation storms

00:00:29.246 --> 00:00:30.713
across much of its surface.

00:00:30.747 --> 00:00:33.147
I estimate that the planet
will be uninhabitable

00:00:33.183 --> 00:00:34.707
in less than 38 hours.

00:00:34.751 --> 00:00:37.219
The distress call
came in only four days ago.

00:00:37.254 --> 00:00:39.722
Why would Dr. Rozhenko
have waited so long

00:00:39.756 --> 00:00:41.053
before sending it?

00:00:41.091 --> 00:00:42.388
Atmospheric dissipation

00:00:42.426 --> 00:00:45.122
is a rare and essentially
unpredictable event.

00:00:45.162 --> 00:00:47.460
When it occurs,
it proceeds rapidly.

00:00:47.497 --> 00:00:50.830
Dr. Rozhenko may not have
had sufficient warning.

00:00:50.867 --> 00:00:52.334
What was that?

00:00:52.369 --> 00:00:54.837
The dissipation effect

00:00:54.871 --> 00:00:57.101
is generating
plasmonic energy bursts.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:59.335
Is there any danger to the ship?

00:00:59.376 --> 00:01:00.843
I do not believe so.

00:01:00.877 --> 00:01:03.277
However, we may experience
intermittent system failures

00:01:03.313 --> 00:01:05.281
and power surges as a result.

00:01:05.315 --> 00:01:07.647
Keep an eye on it.

00:01:07.684 --> 00:01:09.151
Mr. Worf, any luck?

00:01:09.186 --> 00:01:12.155
There is still no response
to our hails, sir.

00:01:12.189 --> 00:01:14.680
I'm attempting to scan
the observation post.

00:01:14.725 --> 00:01:16.192
He could be hurt.

00:01:16.226 --> 00:01:17.693
Maybe he can't respond.

00:01:17.728 --> 00:01:20.390
Sensor interference
is significant

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:22.830
but the post appears
to be intact.

00:01:22.866 --> 00:01:25.391
Their power grid
is still functioning.

00:01:25.435 --> 00:01:28.063
However, I am reading
no life-forms

00:01:28.105 --> 00:01:29.572
within the structure.

00:01:29.606 --> 00:01:32.074
It's not like him
to leave the post.

00:01:32.109 --> 00:01:33.770
Especially
under these circumstances.

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:36.779
Captain, I'm detecting
faint power emissions

00:01:36.813 --> 00:01:39.281
from a system of caverns
near the post.

00:01:39.316 --> 00:01:41.307
It could be a deflector shield.

00:01:41.351 --> 00:01:43.342
They can't be native
to the planet.

00:01:43.387 --> 00:01:44.786
The Boraalans don't have

00:01:44.821 --> 00:01:47.346
anything close to that
level of technology.

00:01:47.391 --> 00:01:49.450
Captain, request permission
to lead an away team.

00:01:51.495 --> 00:01:52.792
Very well.

00:01:52.829 --> 00:01:55.525
But regardless of this
planet's immediate situation

00:01:55.565 --> 00:01:57.692
we must observe
the Prime Directive.

00:01:57.734 --> 00:01:59.531
I want to minimize

00:01:59.569 --> 00:02:03.027
the risk of contact
with the inhabitants.

00:02:03.073 --> 00:02:04.734
You will go down alone, Mr. Worf

00:02:04.775 --> 00:02:06.504
and I want to have you
surgically altered

00:02:06.543 --> 00:02:08.238
so that you could pass
as a Boraalan.

00:02:08.278 --> 00:02:10.109
Aye, sir.

00:02:17.554 --> 00:02:21.183
You're worried about Nikolai,
aren't you?

00:02:21.224 --> 00:02:23.021
Yes.

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:25.551
Are the two of you close?

00:02:25.595 --> 00:02:29.031
We are brothers.

00:02:29.066 --> 00:02:31.125
You never talk much about him.

00:02:31.168 --> 00:02:32.635
What's he like?

00:02:32.669 --> 00:02:35.900
Nikolai is older than I

00:02:35.939 --> 00:02:38.908
and we are not alike.

00:02:38.942 --> 00:02:42.571
We had many disagreements
when we were growing up.

00:02:42.612 --> 00:02:44.580
That's not unusual.

00:02:44.614 --> 00:02:48.072
Nikolai has a mind of his own.

00:02:48.118 --> 00:02:50.916
He attended Starfleet Academy

00:02:50.954 --> 00:02:54.515
but he was unable
to follow the rules.

00:02:54.558 --> 00:02:57.550
He left after one year.

00:02:59.229 --> 00:03:01.857
But he has many fine qualities.

00:03:01.898 --> 00:03:04.264
He's brilliant, persuasive...

00:03:04.301 --> 00:03:06.269
a natural leader.

00:03:06.303 --> 00:03:07.861
Sounds intriguing.

00:03:07.971 --> 00:03:11.134
I look forward to meeting him.

00:03:33.396 --> 00:03:35.591
What are you doing here?

00:03:38.735 --> 00:03:40.396
You're not from our village.

00:03:40.437 --> 00:03:43.235
Who are you?

00:03:43.273 --> 00:03:45.264
Who is this?

00:03:47.144 --> 00:03:49.237
My name is Worf.

00:03:49.279 --> 00:03:51.543
I am a traveler.

00:03:51.581 --> 00:03:54.049
How did you survive the storms?

00:03:54.084 --> 00:03:56.484
I would know that voice
anywhere.

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:59.011
Worf, is it really you?

00:04:01.558 --> 00:04:04.026
It's good to see you.

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:07.223
You've changed a lot
in four years.

00:04:07.264 --> 00:04:09.061
Nikolai?

00:04:09.099 --> 00:04:10.259
Yes.

00:04:11.801 --> 00:04:13.291
Oh, Worf.

00:04:13.336 --> 00:04:15.270
This is my brother Worf.
He's come to help us.

00:04:49.239 --> 00:04:53.642
Space, the final frontier.

00:04:53.677 --> 00:04:57.511
These are the voyages
of the Starship Enterprise.

00:04:57.547 --> 00:04:59.515
Its continuing mission...

00:04:59.549 --> 00:05:03.417
to explore strange new worlds

00:05:03.453 --> 00:05:07.856
to seek out new life
and new civilizations

00:05:07.924 --> 00:05:12.486
to boldly go
where no one has gone before.

00:06:10.453 --> 00:06:13.286
But if you were able to get here
the storms must have subsided.

00:06:13.322 --> 00:06:14.516
Please...

00:06:14.557 --> 00:06:17.048
Do you think it's safe enough
to return to the surface?

00:06:17.093 --> 00:06:19.425
Please, I must speak
to my brother.

00:06:24.066 --> 00:06:27.194
Nikolai, what have you done?

00:06:27.236 --> 00:06:28.362
They were dying.

00:06:28.404 --> 00:06:31.032
I refused to sit there
safe in that observation post

00:06:31.073 --> 00:06:32.404
and watch it happen.

00:06:32.441 --> 00:06:34.409
I set up a deflector shield

00:06:34.443 --> 00:06:36.570
to screen these caves
from the radiation

00:06:36.612 --> 00:06:37.874
and then I brought them here.

00:06:37.947 --> 00:06:39.414
What did you tell them?

00:06:39.448 --> 00:06:40.574
They think I'm a Boraalan.

00:06:40.616 --> 00:06:42.880
I told them I was from
another village far from here.

00:06:42.985 --> 00:06:44.714
Well, at least you
had that much sense.

00:06:44.754 --> 00:06:46.085
When I sent the distress call

00:06:46.122 --> 00:06:47.885
I knew the Enterprise
was in this sector

00:06:47.957 --> 00:06:49.891
but I wasn't sure
you'd be the one to come.

00:06:49.925 --> 00:06:51.517
I'm so glad
that you're here, Worf.

00:06:51.560 --> 00:06:56.088
Nikolai, there is nothing
we can do for these people.

00:06:57.600 --> 00:07:00.296
You have only postponed
their deaths.

00:07:00.336 --> 00:07:02.531
I want to discuss that
with your Captain.

00:07:02.571 --> 00:07:07.304
And I am certain
he will want to speak with you.

00:07:07.343 --> 00:07:09.743
Friends, my brother and I
must go back to the surface.

00:07:09.779 --> 00:07:12.270
He has provisions and will
need help bringing them here.

00:07:12.314 --> 00:07:13.645
We will return shortly.

00:07:13.682 --> 00:07:14.808
It's too dangerous.

00:07:14.850 --> 00:07:16.442
The storms can occur
without warning.

00:07:16.485 --> 00:07:17.577
If you're caught in one...

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:18.814
Don't worry.
Worf is a seer.

00:07:18.854 --> 00:07:21.322
He understands the nature
of the storms.

00:07:21.357 --> 00:07:24.383
He'll know
when it's safe to travel.

00:07:24.426 --> 00:07:25.393
Yes.

00:07:25.427 --> 00:07:26.860
That is correct.

00:07:26.929 --> 00:07:29.625
Our seer died
when the storms first came.

00:07:29.665 --> 00:07:31.633
We've been without his guidance

00:07:31.667 --> 00:07:33.134
for many weeks.

00:07:33.169 --> 00:07:34.659
Let me go with you.

00:07:34.703 --> 00:07:36.796
I know the terrain
better than anyone

00:07:36.839 --> 00:07:38.136
and I can help.

00:07:38.174 --> 00:07:39.141
No, Vorin.

00:07:39.175 --> 00:07:41.143
Worf and I will be safe.

00:07:41.177 --> 00:07:42.576
We'll return shortly.

00:07:49.819 --> 00:07:51.286
Doctor, you were fully aware

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:54.118
that the atmospheric dissipation
could not be stopped.

00:07:54.156 --> 00:07:57.489
What did you hope to accomplish
by assisting these people?

00:07:57.526 --> 00:07:59.994
I was trying to give
them a future.

00:08:00.029 --> 00:08:02.691
What I propose is

00:08:02.731 --> 00:08:04.824
we create an atmospheric shield
on the planet.

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:06.026
We can camouflage the equipment

00:08:06.068 --> 00:08:07.695
just as was done
with my observation post.

00:08:07.736 --> 00:08:09.601
No one will ever know
it's there.

00:08:09.638 --> 00:08:10.832
You can't be serious.

00:08:10.906 --> 00:08:12.032
Indeed, I am.

00:08:12.074 --> 00:08:13.735
I realize it will
only provide atmosphere

00:08:13.776 --> 00:08:15.744
for a limited area
on the surface

00:08:15.778 --> 00:08:18.838
but it will be enough
to save one village.

00:08:18.948 --> 00:08:21.314
I have no intention of
compounding what you have done

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:23.011
by committing
another gross violation

00:08:23.052 --> 00:08:24.178
of the Prime Directive.

00:08:24.220 --> 00:08:27.087
Captain, the Boraalans have

00:08:27.122 --> 00:08:30.853
a rich and beautiful culture,
a deep spiritual life.

00:08:30.926 --> 00:08:33.053
They deserve the chance
to survive

00:08:33.095 --> 00:08:35.495
and isn't that
what the Prime Directive

00:08:35.531 --> 00:08:37.328
was truly intended to do...

00:08:37.366 --> 00:08:39.994
to allow cultures to survive
and grow naturally?

00:08:40.035 --> 00:08:41.002
Not exactly.

00:08:41.036 --> 00:08:43.027
The Prime Directive was designed

00:08:43.072 --> 00:08:44.733
to insure noninterference.

00:08:44.773 --> 00:08:47.435
But aren't we interfering
either way?

00:08:47.476 --> 00:08:48.807
If we take no action

00:08:48.844 --> 00:08:51.335
it's a conscious decision
to let the Boraalans die.

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:52.506
Exactly.

00:08:52.548 --> 00:08:55.176
We have the power
to save some of them.

00:08:55.217 --> 00:08:56.878
All we have to do
is exercise it.

00:08:56.986 --> 00:08:59.147
We are sworn
to uphold the principle

00:08:59.188 --> 00:09:00.246
of the Prime Directive.

00:09:00.289 --> 00:09:01.483
And until that is changed

00:09:01.523 --> 00:09:04.151
there is no further course
of action that we can take.

00:09:04.193 --> 00:09:05.182
Is that understood?

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:10.198
Some of my...

00:09:10.232 --> 00:09:14.396
Iog recorders are still
in my observation post.

00:09:14.436 --> 00:09:15.926
They contain
most of my research.

00:09:15.971 --> 00:09:18.997
Since it appears
that the only way

00:09:19.041 --> 00:09:22.010
I'm going to preserve
the Boraalan culture

00:09:22.044 --> 00:09:23.409
is in a museum...

00:09:23.445 --> 00:09:25.845
I request permission

00:09:25.881 --> 00:09:27.746
to return to the surface
and retrieve them.

00:09:27.783 --> 00:09:30.081
I'm afraid
that won't be possible.

00:09:30.119 --> 00:09:32.553
But you can have full use
of the ship's computer

00:09:32.588 --> 00:09:34.556
to set up a com link

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:37.024
and upload your data from here.

00:09:37.059 --> 00:09:40.051
If there's nothing further,
you're dismissed.

00:09:49.738 --> 00:09:52.639
I am sorry, Nikolai.

00:09:52.675 --> 00:09:55.269
I wish there were another way.

00:10:01.650 --> 00:10:02.878
I am quite familiar

00:10:02.918 --> 00:10:05.045
with your communications
systems.

00:10:05.087 --> 00:10:09.251
If you like, I will help you
set up your com link.

00:10:12.027 --> 00:10:14.018
I'll do it myself.

00:10:16.899 --> 00:10:20.266
Captain, atmospheric
dissipation has accelerated

00:10:20.302 --> 00:10:22.463
over the past several hours.

00:10:22.504 --> 00:10:24.870
I estimate
the planet's atmosphere

00:10:24.907 --> 00:10:27.375
will be completely gone
within three minutes.

00:10:27.409 --> 00:10:30.276
Captain, I've completed
my data uplink.

00:10:30.312 --> 00:10:33.338
With your permission,
I would like to integrate

00:10:33.382 --> 00:10:36.317
my research logs with the ship's
library computer.

00:10:36.352 --> 00:10:38.752
Of course.

00:10:38.787 --> 00:10:40.914
The mesosphere is gone, sir.

00:10:41.023 --> 00:10:42.923
Plasmonic reactions
are now beginning

00:10:43.025 --> 00:10:44.925
to break down the troposphere.

00:10:45.027 --> 00:10:48.121
Put it on screen.

00:10:54.169 --> 00:10:56.330
What's going on?

00:10:56.372 --> 00:10:57.805
It appears
the plasmonic reactions

00:10:57.840 --> 00:10:59.740
are continuing to interfere
with our sensors.

00:10:59.775 --> 00:11:01.470
I thought you had compensated
for that.

00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:02.807
I had, sir.

00:11:02.845 --> 00:11:05.871
I will attempt to engage
additional filtering elements.

00:11:08.550 --> 00:11:10.381
Visual reestablished.

00:11:15.090 --> 00:11:20.289
This is one of those times...

00:11:20.329 --> 00:11:23.321
when we must face
the ramifications

00:11:23.365 --> 00:11:25.333
of the Prime Directive

00:11:25.367 --> 00:11:28.700
and honor those lives
which we cannot save.

00:11:28.737 --> 00:11:32.605
I find no honor in this
whatsoever, Captain.

00:11:35.044 --> 00:11:38.036
You will forgive me
if I don't stay.

00:11:58.634 --> 00:12:01.330
You have the Bridge, Number One.

00:12:01.370 --> 00:12:04.339
Helm, take us out of orbit.

00:12:04.373 --> 00:12:07.342
Set a course for Starbase 87,
warp five.

00:12:07.376 --> 00:12:09.367
Aye, sir.

00:12:12.114 --> 00:12:13.513
What happened?

00:12:13.549 --> 00:12:16.017
There appears to be
an unusual power drain

00:12:16.051 --> 00:12:18.019
in the EPS distribution net.

00:12:18.053 --> 00:12:19.247
What's the source?

00:12:19.288 --> 00:12:20.255
Unknown, sir.

00:12:20.289 --> 00:12:21.688
It is difficult to localize.

00:12:21.723 --> 00:12:23.691
The power drain is registered

00:12:23.725 --> 00:12:25.022
on my security grid as well,
sir.

00:12:25.060 --> 00:12:27.290
It appears to be coming
from deck ten.

00:12:27.329 --> 00:12:28.455
All right, Mr. Worf

00:12:28.497 --> 00:12:30.465
get a security team on it.

00:12:30.499 --> 00:12:31.591
Aye, sir.

00:12:33.635 --> 00:12:37.628
Concentrate your scans
on the EPS transfer links.

00:12:50.552 --> 00:12:54.010
Computer, open Holodeck Five.

00:12:54.056 --> 00:12:56.024
Unable to comply.

00:12:56.058 --> 00:12:58.185
Holodeck Five is in use.

00:12:58.227 --> 00:12:59.524
Override.

00:12:59.561 --> 00:13:02.325
Authorization:
Worf-theta-six-one-nine.

00:13:02.364 --> 00:13:04.332
Unable to comply.

00:13:04.366 --> 00:13:08.359
Holodeck control systems
have been bypassed.

00:13:17.112 --> 00:13:19.103
Worf, come in.

00:13:27.589 --> 00:13:29.420
Nikolai?

00:13:29.458 --> 00:13:31.289
What are you doing here?

00:13:31.326 --> 00:13:33.794
I have something to show you.

00:13:33.829 --> 00:13:36.821
Whatever you do, stay quiet.

00:13:39.935 --> 00:13:41.300
Look.

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:54.149
I've done
what you refused to do.

00:13:54.183 --> 00:13:56.947
I've saved them.

00:14:03.225 --> 00:14:05.125
I started thinking about this
days ago

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:06.957
when it became clear
the planet was doomed.

00:14:06.995 --> 00:14:09.862
I knew if I could gain access
to your ship's computer

00:14:09.931 --> 00:14:11.865
I could generate a replica
of the caves.

00:14:11.900 --> 00:14:14.869
The hard part was transporting
the Boraalans into the holodeck

00:14:14.970 --> 00:14:17.063
without anybody
on the Enterprise noticing.

00:14:17.105 --> 00:14:19.005
But I was able
to blank out the sensors

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:20.564
and make it look
like interference

00:14:20.609 --> 00:14:21.803
from the plasmonic bursts.

00:14:21.843 --> 00:14:23.606
And it worked...
perfectly.

00:14:23.645 --> 00:14:26.546
The Boraalans were transported
while they were sleeping.

00:14:26.581 --> 00:14:28.378
They never knew
anything had happened.

00:14:30.051 --> 00:14:32.246
Bridge.

00:14:32.287 --> 00:14:33.618
It's a simple plan, really.

00:14:33.655 --> 00:14:34.849
That's the beauty of it.

00:14:34.889 --> 00:14:35.878
Worf, trust me.

00:14:35.957 --> 00:14:37.891
This is going to work.

00:14:37.959 --> 00:14:39.824
Trust you?

00:14:39.861 --> 00:14:43.422
You never had any intention
of obeying the Captain.

00:14:43.465 --> 00:14:45.456
I wasn't going to let
those people die

00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:47.400
just because your Captain
started quoting

00:14:47.435 --> 00:14:48.527
Federation dogma to me.

00:14:48.570 --> 00:14:51.471
Your duty was to respect
the Captain's orders

00:14:51.506 --> 00:14:53.667
and to uphold
the Prime Directive.

00:14:53.708 --> 00:14:55.539
Duty?

00:14:55.577 --> 00:14:58.011
That's all that really
matters to you, isn't it?

00:14:58.046 --> 00:15:00.537
Well, I refuse to be bound
by an abstraction.

00:15:00.582 --> 00:15:02.641
The lives of the people
of Boraal

00:15:02.684 --> 00:15:04.174
are far more important to me.

00:15:04.219 --> 00:15:06.847
You worry too much, Worf.
You always did.

00:15:06.921 --> 00:15:10.118
Everything will work out.

00:15:10.158 --> 00:15:12.626
You have disgraced yourself.

00:15:12.661 --> 00:15:15.027
And you have disgraced me.

00:15:15.063 --> 00:15:18.226
And I want nothing more
to do with you.

00:15:21.936 --> 00:15:23.767
You realize your career
is finished.

00:15:23.805 --> 00:15:24.863
I know that, Captain.

00:15:24.906 --> 00:15:26.134
I would do it all again.

00:15:26.174 --> 00:15:28.005
What do you expect us
to do now?

00:15:28.043 --> 00:15:30.568
You have left us
with a colony of Boraalans

00:15:30.612 --> 00:15:32.807
who think they're still
on their own planet.

00:15:32.847 --> 00:15:34.747
I didn't beam them up
without a plan.

00:15:34.783 --> 00:15:36.273
I've given this
a lot of thought.

00:15:36.318 --> 00:15:39.583
I think we can find
a new planet, an M-Class world

00:15:39.621 --> 00:15:40.747
that can be their new home.

00:15:40.789 --> 00:15:42.882
A home which would look
very different from Boraal.

00:15:42.924 --> 00:15:45.119
You can't really believe
that they'll be fooled.

00:15:45.160 --> 00:15:47.025
That's where the holodeck
comes in.

00:15:47.062 --> 00:15:48.529
I'll go back
and tell the Boraalans

00:15:48.563 --> 00:15:49.723
we're going on a journey

00:15:49.764 --> 00:15:52.494
to a different place where
they'll be safe from the storms.

00:15:52.534 --> 00:15:56.231
The holodeck can gradually
change the terrain as we travel

00:15:56.271 --> 00:15:58.535
so that, in the end,
the holodeck simulation

00:15:58.573 --> 00:16:00.905
will match the conditions
on the new planet.

00:16:00.942 --> 00:16:04.605
Then we'll simply
beam them down.

00:16:04.646 --> 00:16:07.137
What if it doesn't work?

00:16:07.182 --> 00:16:09.150
What if they become aware

00:16:09.184 --> 00:16:11.846
that something strange
is going on?

00:16:11.886 --> 00:16:14.286
Captain, I can't prepare
for every contingency

00:16:14.322 --> 00:16:17.086
but I assure you, I'm accustomed
to thinking on my feet.

00:16:17.125 --> 00:16:20.026
I'll deal with the situation
as it evolves.

00:16:23.331 --> 00:16:26.960
I'm not enthusiastic
about this plan

00:16:27.001 --> 00:16:30.801
but I don't see
that we have another option.

00:16:30.839 --> 00:16:33.307
Very well, let's give it a try.

00:16:33.341 --> 00:16:36.139
Thank you, Captain.

00:16:40.181 --> 00:16:41.739
There are countless
M-Class planets

00:16:41.783 --> 00:16:44.115
in Federation space
that can support the Boraalans.

00:16:44.152 --> 00:16:45.642
We need to narrow
the parameters.

00:16:47.922 --> 00:16:49.480
To complete the analysis.

00:16:49.524 --> 00:16:51.424
Even then, there's no guarantee

00:16:51.459 --> 00:16:53.154
that we'll find
a suitable planet.

00:16:53.194 --> 00:16:54.388
That is correct, sir.

00:16:54.429 --> 00:16:57.262
Captain, you'd better
take a look at this.

00:16:57.298 --> 00:16:58.424
What is it?

00:16:58.466 --> 00:16:59.797
We've got a problem, sir.

00:16:59.834 --> 00:17:02.132
I don't think
it's going to be possible

00:17:02.170 --> 00:17:03.831
to keep this holodeck
simulation stable.

00:17:03.905 --> 00:17:04.837
Why not?

00:17:04.906 --> 00:17:06.203
The plasmonic energy bursts

00:17:06.241 --> 00:17:08.471
from the planet are affecting
the ship's systems.

00:17:08.510 --> 00:17:10.444
We're having problems
with the EPS systems

00:17:10.478 --> 00:17:12.036
and the power
distribution matrix.

00:17:12.080 --> 00:17:13.445
And as a result

00:17:13.481 --> 00:17:16.848
the holodeck imaging processor
has been severely destabilized.

00:17:16.918 --> 00:17:19.819
It's not a question
of whether the simulation

00:17:19.854 --> 00:17:21.287
will break down,
it's a question of when.

00:17:21.322 --> 00:17:22.414
There's no way around it?

00:17:22.457 --> 00:17:23.515
Not while it's running.

00:17:23.558 --> 00:17:24.525
In order to fix it

00:17:24.559 --> 00:17:26.390
I'd have to shut down
all of the holodecks

00:17:26.428 --> 00:17:28.760
and re-initialize
the entire system.

00:17:28.797 --> 00:17:30.424
That will take hours.

00:17:30.465 --> 00:17:33.229
We'll just have to hope the
simulation holds long enough.

00:17:34.836 --> 00:17:36.531
Very well, let's try it.

00:17:36.571 --> 00:17:38.198
Mr. La Forge, I want you
to monitor

00:17:38.239 --> 00:17:39.570
the situation very carefully

00:17:39.607 --> 00:17:41.666
and keep an open com link
with the holodeck

00:17:41.709 --> 00:17:43.973
so as to be apprised
of any problems.

00:17:44.012 --> 00:17:45.036
Aye, sir.

00:17:45.079 --> 00:17:46.740
Captain, I'll return
to the holodeck

00:17:46.781 --> 00:17:49.045
as soon as my surgical
alterations are completed

00:17:49.083 --> 00:17:51.415
and I'll prepare the Boraalans
for their journey.

00:17:51.453 --> 00:17:52.818
Considering the situation

00:17:52.854 --> 00:17:54.412
you have put us in,
I don't think it's wise

00:17:54.456 --> 00:17:55.787
to leave you alone
with those people.

00:17:55.824 --> 00:17:56.916
Mr. Worf will accompany you.

00:17:58.793 --> 00:18:02.024
Sir, perhaps someone else
would be a better choice.

00:18:02.063 --> 00:18:04.224
Counselor Troi
is familiar with...

00:18:04.265 --> 00:18:06.233
Mr. Worf, the Boraalans
already know you.

00:18:06.267 --> 00:18:08.667
There's no need to introduce
them to anyone new.

00:18:10.305 --> 00:18:11.772
Aye, sir.

00:18:15.844 --> 00:18:18.005
Keep a close eye
on your brother.

00:18:18.046 --> 00:18:21.812
I don't want him making
the situation worse than it is.

00:18:31.593 --> 00:18:34.153
My friends, we have returned.

00:18:35.330 --> 00:18:36.820
We have food.

00:18:40.535 --> 00:18:44.471
This is difficult to say,
but you have a right to hear it.

00:18:44.506 --> 00:18:47.998
By the time Worf and I
had reached the surface

00:18:48.042 --> 00:18:49.600
the village was gone.

00:18:49.644 --> 00:18:51.703
The storms have
destroyed everything.

00:18:51.746 --> 00:18:53.839
There is nothing left
for us to return to.

00:18:53.882 --> 00:18:55.509
We can't survive in here.

00:18:55.550 --> 00:18:56.881
Our supplies won't last forever.

00:18:56.985 --> 00:18:58.179
That's why we must leave.

00:18:58.219 --> 00:19:01.279
There is a place far from here
where there are no storms.

00:19:01.322 --> 00:19:03.654
It will be a difficult journey

00:19:03.691 --> 00:19:05.659
but, in the end,
we will have a new home.

00:19:05.693 --> 00:19:07.991
I know a way through the caves.

00:19:08.029 --> 00:19:11.328
We will travel safely
until we return to the surface.

00:19:11.366 --> 00:19:12.765
Where is this new land?

00:19:12.800 --> 00:19:13.824
As we said

00:19:13.902 --> 00:19:15.392
it is far from here.

00:19:15.436 --> 00:19:18.098
It will not be like
the home you knew.

00:19:18.139 --> 00:19:20.198
Even the stars may be different.

00:19:20.241 --> 00:19:23.608
Why would they be different,
and how do you know

00:19:23.645 --> 00:19:25.374
we'll be safe there?

00:19:25.413 --> 00:19:26.471
My brother is a seer.

00:19:26.514 --> 00:19:27.538
If he says we'll be safe

00:19:27.582 --> 00:19:29.140
you must trust that
we will be safe.

00:19:34.422 --> 00:19:35.446
What's wrong?

00:19:35.490 --> 00:19:36.548
Look!

00:19:43.798 --> 00:19:45.095
Do not worry.

00:19:45.133 --> 00:19:46.828
It is an omen.

00:19:48.036 --> 00:19:49.560
What does it mean?

00:19:51.739 --> 00:19:53.434
It is the sign...

00:19:54.609 --> 00:19:56.304
of La Forge.

00:19:56.344 --> 00:19:58.505
It is a message to travelers.

00:19:58.546 --> 00:20:03.347
It is said when these lines
appear and disappear in a pool

00:20:03.384 --> 00:20:05.409
of water, the road ahead

00:20:05.453 --> 00:20:08.081
will be filled
with good fortune.

00:20:08.122 --> 00:20:10.249
Hang in there, Worf.

00:20:10.291 --> 00:20:12.919
Give me just a second...

00:20:17.532 --> 00:20:18.897
There.

00:20:19.000 --> 00:20:20.729
That should do it.

00:20:29.611 --> 00:20:32.307
You see?
Our journey is already blessed.

00:20:32.347 --> 00:20:34.144
The road ahead is long.

00:20:34.182 --> 00:20:36.309
Let us have a meal together

00:20:36.351 --> 00:20:38.819
then we'll make
preparations to leave.

00:20:43.424 --> 00:20:45.187
Worf, very good work.

00:20:45.226 --> 00:20:48.923
Apparently, we don't make
such a bad team after all.

00:20:49.030 --> 00:20:51.760
We are not a team.

00:20:51.799 --> 00:20:55.064
I am here because Captain
Picard ordered me here.

00:20:55.103 --> 00:20:57.537
Worf, don't we both
share the same goal?

00:20:57.572 --> 00:20:59.767
Aren't we both trying
to make this plan work?

00:20:59.807 --> 00:21:01.502
Only because you
forced us into it.

00:21:01.542 --> 00:21:03.009
I'm not ashamed of what I did.

00:21:03.044 --> 00:21:04.739
I'm not sorry
I saved their lives.

00:21:06.314 --> 00:21:07.872
You have not changed.

00:21:07.915 --> 00:21:09.473
You still expect people

00:21:09.517 --> 00:21:11.678
to solve the problems
you create.

00:21:11.719 --> 00:21:14.813
I'm not here to work out
the issues of our childhood.

00:21:14.856 --> 00:21:17.154
I'm here to save a people
who I care about

00:21:17.191 --> 00:21:20.524
and if that upsets you,
then so be it.

00:21:26.234 --> 00:21:27.895
These are the two planets

00:21:27.935 --> 00:21:29.994
which best match
our search criteria.

00:21:30.038 --> 00:21:31.266
Draygo IV features

00:21:31.305 --> 00:21:33.330
an unusually large
temperate zone.

00:21:33.374 --> 00:21:35.740
However, it is
within three light-years

00:21:35.777 --> 00:21:37.108
of Cardassian space.

00:21:37.145 --> 00:21:40.444
There are constant border
disputes in that sector.

00:21:40.481 --> 00:21:42.540
The alternative is Vacca VI.

00:21:42.583 --> 00:21:45.108
It is located
in the Cabral sector.

00:21:45.153 --> 00:21:46.620
That's pretty isolated.

00:21:46.654 --> 00:21:48.918
It offers
a less hospitable climate

00:21:48.956 --> 00:21:51.220
than the Boraalans
are accustomed to.

00:21:51.259 --> 00:21:53.591
However, it would
still appear to be

00:21:53.628 --> 00:21:54.788
the better choice.

00:21:54.829 --> 00:21:56.456
Do you disagree, Doctor?

00:21:56.497 --> 00:21:57.759
No, Data, you're right.

00:21:57.799 --> 00:21:59.266
It's just that the enormity

00:21:59.300 --> 00:22:01.234
of what we're doing
is overwhelming.

00:22:01.269 --> 00:22:03.669
We are deciding the future
of a species.

00:22:03.705 --> 00:22:05.866
It is a formidable
responsibility.

00:22:05.940 --> 00:22:08.875
There are so many questions
we don't have answers to.

00:22:08.943 --> 00:22:12.312
What if the climate is so
different that it affects them

00:22:12.445 --> 00:22:14.003
in a way
that we can't anticipate?

00:22:14.047 --> 00:22:16.447
How do we even know
they'll be able to survive?

00:22:16.482 --> 00:22:19.280
And if they do, how would
their society evolve

00:22:19.319 --> 00:22:22.413
and what impact will it have
on the Vaccan system?

00:22:22.455 --> 00:22:24.787
We have no idea
what this decision

00:22:24.824 --> 00:22:26.689
will mean to their future.

00:22:26.726 --> 00:22:29.490
Doctor, I do not believe
we can offer any guarantees.

00:22:29.529 --> 00:22:31.292
We can simply make
the best choice

00:22:31.331 --> 00:22:32.525
we have at the moment.

00:22:34.834 --> 00:22:36.734
All right, Data.

00:22:36.769 --> 00:22:38.669
Vacca VI it is.

00:22:38.705 --> 00:22:39.899
Data to Bridge.

00:22:39.972 --> 00:22:41.269
Picard here.

00:22:41.307 --> 00:22:44.299
We have located a new home
for the Boraalans, sir.

00:22:44.344 --> 00:22:48.280
It is Vacca VI
in the Cabral sector.

00:22:48.314 --> 00:22:52.273
We can reach that in 42 hours
at maximum warp, sir.

00:22:52.318 --> 00:22:53.444
Very well.

00:22:53.486 --> 00:22:55.920
Helm, set course for Vacca VI.

00:22:55.988 --> 00:22:57.319
Aye, sir.

00:23:27.920 --> 00:23:29.319
What is this?

00:23:30.690 --> 00:23:32.089
Our Chronicle.

00:23:32.125 --> 00:23:36.152
The history of our village?

00:23:36.195 --> 00:23:38.595
Doesn't your village
keep a Chronicle?

00:23:38.631 --> 00:23:39.996
Not in this manner.

00:23:40.032 --> 00:23:41.090
Then how do

00:23:41.134 --> 00:23:43.125
you teach your children
their history...

00:23:43.169 --> 00:23:46.104
who their ancestors were,
where they come from?

00:23:46.139 --> 00:23:50.269
We tell each other stories...

00:23:50.309 --> 00:23:51.776
make up songs.

00:23:53.479 --> 00:23:57.813
Stories change with each person
who tells them

00:23:57.850 --> 00:24:02.287
but this... this will always
be the same.

00:24:02.321 --> 00:24:05.290
Our Chronicle
has been maintained

00:24:05.324 --> 00:24:08.054
for 17 generations.

00:24:08.094 --> 00:24:12.053
I was only able to save
the last six.

00:24:12.098 --> 00:24:17.536
This shows the destruction
of our village.

00:24:18.871 --> 00:24:23.001
This is you and Nikolai
leading us to safety.

00:24:29.449 --> 00:24:30.882
We must leave.

00:24:30.983 --> 00:24:32.678
Gather your belongings.

00:24:42.395 --> 00:24:44.693
One of the scrolls is gone.

00:24:44.730 --> 00:24:47.358
I must have dropped it
in the passageway.

00:24:47.400 --> 00:24:49.231
I'll go find it.

00:24:50.536 --> 00:24:52.595
We must stay together.

00:24:52.638 --> 00:24:55.038
You will have
to leave it behind.

00:24:55.074 --> 00:24:58.874
Worf, the Chronicle
is the life of our village.

00:24:58.911 --> 00:25:02.745
Without that past,
our future means nothing.

00:25:02.782 --> 00:25:04.545
I must find it.

00:25:06.052 --> 00:25:07.178
Go.

00:25:07.220 --> 00:25:08.482
And return quickly.

00:25:14.894 --> 00:25:16.293
Seer.

00:25:17.797 --> 00:25:19.355
I am an old man.

00:25:19.398 --> 00:25:21.764
Would you help me with my gear?

00:25:21.801 --> 00:25:23.132
Of course.

00:25:28.174 --> 00:25:31.769
That is Tarrana, my daughter.

00:25:31.811 --> 00:25:36.077
I am fortunate she was old
enough to survive the storms.

00:25:36.115 --> 00:25:37.776
She is a fine girl.

00:25:37.817 --> 00:25:40.581
Oh, she is a beautiful girl.

00:25:40.620 --> 00:25:43.214
She has not been
promised to anyone.

00:25:43.256 --> 00:25:47.590
If I do not reach our new home

00:25:47.627 --> 00:25:50.755
I would like her
to become your wife.

00:25:57.470 --> 00:26:00.906
You will reach your new home.

00:26:00.940 --> 00:26:02.168
I promise.

00:27:41.340 --> 00:27:43.831
Can I help you?

00:27:49.148 --> 00:27:50.115
You okay?

00:27:50.149 --> 00:27:51.446
Do you need some help?

00:27:52.585 --> 00:27:54.485
It's okay.

00:27:54.520 --> 00:27:57.387
Take it easy.

00:27:57.423 --> 00:27:59.983
All right, everybody, back off.
Back off.

00:28:09.935 --> 00:28:13.166
I know things must look
very strange to you

00:28:13.205 --> 00:28:16.265
but everything's going
to be all right.

00:28:16.308 --> 00:28:20.176
No one's going to hurt you.

00:28:20.212 --> 00:28:23.841
We're friends
of Nikolai and Worf.

00:28:23.949 --> 00:28:26.042
Don't be afraid.

00:28:26.085 --> 00:28:27.382
Nikolai?

00:28:27.420 --> 00:28:29.547
Yes.

00:28:29.588 --> 00:28:35.857
He's my friend,
and that means you are, too.

00:28:35.961 --> 00:28:37.258
I promise.

00:28:37.296 --> 00:28:38.820
I won't hurt you.

00:28:38.864 --> 00:28:40.695
Please...

00:28:40.733 --> 00:28:42.724
help me.

00:28:49.709 --> 00:28:51.700
Where am I?

00:28:56.848 --> 00:28:59.339
I'm sorry,
there's nothing I can do.

00:28:59.384 --> 00:29:01.818
His neurophysiology
is very unusual.

00:29:01.920 --> 00:29:03.217
I can't wipe his memory.

00:29:03.254 --> 00:29:04.551
I see.
How is he?

00:29:04.589 --> 00:29:05.920
As well as can be expected.

00:29:05.957 --> 00:29:07.447
I've given him a mild sedative

00:29:07.492 --> 00:29:09.153
and Troi's been
speaking with him

00:29:09.194 --> 00:29:10.752
and he seems much calmer.

00:29:10.795 --> 00:29:12.820
Does he understand
the situation?

00:29:12.864 --> 00:29:14.161
I think so.

00:29:14.199 --> 00:29:15.496
Contact Mr. Worf.

00:29:15.533 --> 00:29:17.933
Make sure that he knows
what's going on.

00:29:19.237 --> 00:29:22.798
Here he is now.

00:29:22.841 --> 00:29:25.036
This is Captain Picard.

00:29:25.076 --> 00:29:27.408
Vorin, isn't it?

00:29:27.445 --> 00:29:30.107
Why did you bring us here?

00:29:30.148 --> 00:29:33.117
Your planet was dying.

00:29:33.151 --> 00:29:35.517
It could no longer support life.

00:29:35.553 --> 00:29:38.021
We took you away from it.

00:29:38.056 --> 00:29:42.083
But... we never left the caves.

00:29:42.127 --> 00:29:47.326
We have the ability to create
the illusion of other places

00:29:47.365 --> 00:29:51.028
like the caves on your planet.

00:29:51.069 --> 00:29:54.698
You've actually spent
the last two days

00:29:54.739 --> 00:29:58.072
here on this starship,
not on Boraal.

00:29:58.109 --> 00:30:04.139
Then our home... is gone.

00:30:05.817 --> 00:30:07.216
Yes.

00:30:07.252 --> 00:30:10.983
Vorin, listen to me.

00:30:11.022 --> 00:30:13.513
We can visit many other worlds.

00:30:13.558 --> 00:30:17.392
We can take you to one
where you can build a new life.

00:30:17.428 --> 00:30:18.895
A new life?

00:30:18.997 --> 00:30:25.197
A chance for your culture,
your people to survive and grow.

00:30:25.236 --> 00:30:32.005
How can we grow when everything
that made us who we are is gone?

00:30:57.101 --> 00:31:00.366
Dobara, you go on ahead.

00:31:09.614 --> 00:31:11.707
I will carry your pack.

00:31:11.749 --> 00:31:13.580
Go join the others.

00:31:13.618 --> 00:31:15.552
Thank you, seer.

00:31:25.330 --> 00:31:29.096
It will be dark soon...
a few hours.

00:31:32.470 --> 00:31:34.335
Would you ask Mr. La Forge

00:31:34.372 --> 00:31:36.863
to create
a suitable campsite for us

00:31:36.908 --> 00:31:38.876
a few kilometers from here?

00:31:38.910 --> 00:31:40.343
What's wrong?

00:31:40.378 --> 00:31:42.676
Vorin has left the holodeck.

00:31:42.714 --> 00:31:44.238
How did he get out?

00:31:44.282 --> 00:31:45.749
I do not know

00:31:45.783 --> 00:31:48.274
but Dr. Crusher cannot
erase his memory.

00:31:48.319 --> 00:31:50.150
What will they do with him?

00:31:50.188 --> 00:31:51.917
They've explained
the situation to him.

00:31:52.023 --> 00:31:53.456
He must make his own decisions.

00:31:53.491 --> 00:31:54.822
Wait.

00:31:54.859 --> 00:31:57.350
Are you saying that if Vorin
wants to come back in here

00:31:57.395 --> 00:31:58.555
they'll let him?

00:31:58.596 --> 00:31:59.893
That is right.

00:31:59.931 --> 00:32:01.865
He is not a prisoner.

00:32:01.933 --> 00:32:03.764
But if he comes back here
and tells the others

00:32:03.801 --> 00:32:05.132
what he has seen
on the Enterprise

00:32:05.169 --> 00:32:06.864
everything we have done
will be for nothing.

00:32:06.971 --> 00:32:08.563
Then you should have
considered that

00:32:08.606 --> 00:32:10.301
before you beamed them on board.

00:32:10.341 --> 00:32:11.330
But you never think

00:32:11.376 --> 00:32:13.139
of the consequences
of your acts.

00:32:13.177 --> 00:32:14.542
If you mean by that
that I'm willing

00:32:14.579 --> 00:32:16.012
to do something
while others hesitate

00:32:16.047 --> 00:32:17.173
that's true.

00:32:17.215 --> 00:32:18.978
Everywhere you go
you create chaos.

00:32:19.017 --> 00:32:21.485
How many times did our parents
lie awake at night

00:32:21.519 --> 00:32:23.714
wondering what kind of trouble
you were in.

00:32:23.755 --> 00:32:26.053
Oh, if only I could
have been like you...

00:32:26.090 --> 00:32:27.580
Worf, the perfect son!

00:32:27.625 --> 00:32:28.887
I was not perfect

00:32:28.927 --> 00:32:31.828
but I was not wild
and disobedient.

00:32:31.863 --> 00:32:33.160
Of course not.

00:32:33.197 --> 00:32:34.425
You were too busy
doing your duty.

00:32:34.465 --> 00:32:36.092
I would rather
be accused of that

00:32:36.134 --> 00:32:38.102
than making our mother weep.

00:32:38.136 --> 00:32:39.467
But I see it is clear

00:32:39.504 --> 00:32:41.199
you have no intention
of changing.

00:32:41.239 --> 00:32:43.264
I see no reason
to discuss it further.

00:33:14.138 --> 00:33:17.335
Commander, the holodeck
malfunctions are increasing.

00:33:17.375 --> 00:33:20.071
I'm running every
stabilization routine I know.

00:33:20.111 --> 00:33:22.773
How much longer
until we reach the new planet?

00:33:22.814 --> 00:33:25.078
We'll be there in less
than eight hours.

00:33:25.116 --> 00:33:27.983
You're just going to have
to hold things together

00:33:28.019 --> 00:33:29.008
a little while longer.

00:33:29.053 --> 00:33:30.350
Someone is coming.

00:33:36.461 --> 00:33:38.759
May I speak with you?

00:33:38.796 --> 00:33:40.787
Yes, of course.

00:33:49.307 --> 00:33:52.401
I don't know
what Nikolai said to you

00:33:52.443 --> 00:33:56.539
but please... forgive him?

00:33:56.581 --> 00:34:00.073
It is an old argument.

00:34:00.118 --> 00:34:03.053
I've never seen him like this.

00:34:03.087 --> 00:34:07.080
He's usually so...
confident, so sure of himself

00:34:07.125 --> 00:34:10.822
but now he seems... different.

00:34:10.862 --> 00:34:13.387
Do you know why?

00:34:15.433 --> 00:34:16.730
No.

00:34:16.768 --> 00:34:18.395
No, I do not.

00:34:18.436 --> 00:34:23.499
Ever since Vorin was lost,
people have been afraid...

00:34:23.541 --> 00:34:26.977
worried that we won't reach
our new home.

00:34:27.011 --> 00:34:30.640
We need Nikolai's strength now
more than ever.

00:34:30.681 --> 00:34:33.377
When the storms
first came to our village

00:34:33.418 --> 00:34:35.249
many of us were ready to die

00:34:35.286 --> 00:34:38.687
but Nikolai refused to let us.

00:34:38.723 --> 00:34:42.215
He gathered us together
and led us into caves.

00:34:42.260 --> 00:34:43.852
He saved us.

00:34:43.895 --> 00:34:48.889
He is a brave
and compassionate man

00:34:48.933 --> 00:34:50.833
and I love him.

00:34:50.868 --> 00:34:53.837
Please...

00:34:53.871 --> 00:34:55.463
go to him?

00:34:55.506 --> 00:34:58.669
Make things right between you.

00:34:58.709 --> 00:35:01.143
I want us to be a family.

00:35:01.179 --> 00:35:03.647
Us?

00:35:03.681 --> 00:35:05.012
Yes.

00:35:05.049 --> 00:35:08.644
I want you to consider
yourself my brother.

00:35:08.686 --> 00:35:10.950
After all...

00:35:15.893 --> 00:35:19.226
...you're going to be
the uncle of my child.

00:35:39.750 --> 00:35:42.378
We are in synchronous orbit
over the beam-down site, sir.

00:35:42.419 --> 00:35:43.386
Good.

00:35:43.420 --> 00:35:44.785
Mr. La Forge, how much longer

00:35:44.822 --> 00:35:46.813
before when can we
transport the Boraalans?

00:35:46.857 --> 00:35:49.690
A few more hours, Captain, but
we've got some problems here.

00:35:49.727 --> 00:35:52.560
I don't think the holodeck's
going to last that long.

00:35:52.596 --> 00:35:54.996
We've had materialization errors
and resolution failures

00:35:55.032 --> 00:35:56.021
all over the place.

00:35:56.066 --> 00:35:57.260
And it's getting worse.

00:35:57.301 --> 00:35:59.792
The simulation could fall apart
any minute.

00:35:59.837 --> 00:36:02.328
We'll have the transporter room
standing by

00:36:02.373 --> 00:36:04.341
but we may have
to transport the Boraalans

00:36:04.375 --> 00:36:05.740
whether you're ready or not.

00:36:05.776 --> 00:36:07.539
Please keep Mr. Worf apprised.

00:36:07.578 --> 00:36:09.045
Aye, sir.

00:36:09.079 --> 00:36:11.445
You have the Bridge, Number One.

00:36:11.482 --> 00:36:14.781
We still have one more
problem to worry about.

00:36:28.932 --> 00:36:30.297
Yes.

00:36:33.170 --> 00:36:36.731
We have arrived at the planet
that I told you about.

00:36:36.774 --> 00:36:38.332
Have you made a decision?

00:36:38.375 --> 00:36:42.243
I believe I would like
to go back to my people.

00:36:43.614 --> 00:36:45.741
I see.

00:36:45.783 --> 00:36:48.183
What do you intend to tell them?

00:36:51.355 --> 00:36:52.845
I don't know.

00:36:55.159 --> 00:36:58.526
If you tell them the truth,
what will happen?

00:36:58.562 --> 00:37:00.154
Will they believe you?

00:37:03.067 --> 00:37:05.535
I'm not sure.

00:37:05.569 --> 00:37:07.935
It is a fantastic story.

00:37:09.306 --> 00:37:11.274
Perhaps they will think

00:37:11.308 --> 00:37:14.300
that you have had
an hallucination

00:37:14.345 --> 00:37:16.279
or that you're insane.

00:37:16.313 --> 00:37:19.942
I don't think I would like
to live the rest of my life

00:37:19.983 --> 00:37:21.780
knowing what I know

00:37:21.819 --> 00:37:23.844
and being regarded as a madman.

00:37:23.921 --> 00:37:25.479
On the other hand

00:37:25.522 --> 00:37:29.014
they may believe
your fantastic story.

00:37:29.059 --> 00:37:31.653
They will learn
about... alien worlds

00:37:31.695 --> 00:37:32.855
starships.

00:37:32.896 --> 00:37:35.421
That would be disastrous.

00:37:35.466 --> 00:37:39.095
It would destroy
everything they believed in.

00:37:43.841 --> 00:37:48.369
I can't tell them the truth

00:37:48.412 --> 00:37:52.872
but I don't think I can live
with a secret.

00:37:53.984 --> 00:37:56.782
Then stay here.

00:37:56.820 --> 00:37:59.948
Make a future for yourself
with us.

00:38:05.863 --> 00:38:07.592
I need some time.

00:38:09.032 --> 00:38:10.624
Please.

00:38:23.947 --> 00:38:26.575
How could you have mated
with a Boraalan?

00:38:26.617 --> 00:38:27.606
What were you thinking?!

00:38:27.651 --> 00:38:29.016
I don't owe you an explanation.

00:38:29.052 --> 00:38:30.986
This is a matter
between Dobara and myself.

00:38:31.021 --> 00:38:33.751
As usual, you are only thinking
of yourself.

00:38:33.791 --> 00:38:35.156
And as usual, you are here

00:38:35.192 --> 00:38:36.989
to point out
the error of my ways.

00:38:37.027 --> 00:38:39.086
You have treated
Dobara with dishonor.

00:38:39.129 --> 00:38:40.096
I have not... I love her

00:38:40.130 --> 00:38:41.620
and we are going
to raise our child together.

00:38:41.665 --> 00:38:42.632
That is not possible!

00:38:42.666 --> 00:38:44.395
I cannot allow you
to remain here.

00:38:44.435 --> 00:38:46.027
You will have to kill me first!

00:38:52.309 --> 00:38:53.367
What does it mean?

00:38:53.410 --> 00:38:54.809
The storms have returned.

00:38:54.845 --> 00:38:56.142
We'll all be killed.

00:38:56.180 --> 00:38:58.045
No, you won't.

00:38:58.081 --> 00:39:00.276
Worf has the power
to end the storms

00:39:00.317 --> 00:39:01.375
once and for all.

00:39:01.418 --> 00:39:04.478
Yes, but everyone must
take shelter in the tents.

00:39:04.521 --> 00:39:06.250
The tents won't protect us.

00:39:06.290 --> 00:39:07.814
Worf will protect you.

00:39:07.858 --> 00:39:08.825
You must trust him.

00:39:08.859 --> 00:39:10.486
Hurry, hurry.
Get to your tents now.

00:39:10.527 --> 00:39:11.926
Commander, It might be helpful

00:39:11.962 --> 00:39:14.590
if you could produce a storm...
wind, lightning and thunder.

00:39:14.631 --> 00:39:16.155
I'll see what I can do.

00:39:24.942 --> 00:39:26.273
Get in! Get in!

00:39:26.310 --> 00:39:28.107
The storm is getting worse!

00:39:30.481 --> 00:39:31.948
Stay inside.

00:39:35.652 --> 00:39:38.143
Worf and I will
take care of you.

00:39:43.660 --> 00:39:45.753
Commander, energize.

00:40:05.249 --> 00:40:09.310
The storms will not return.

00:40:10.687 --> 00:40:15.624
As I said he would, my brother
Worf has saved us all.

00:40:24.334 --> 00:40:28.031
Captain's Log, Stardate 47427.2.

00:40:28.071 --> 00:40:30.369
The Boraalans have safely
reached the site

00:40:30.407 --> 00:40:32.807
of what will eventually
become their new village.

00:40:32.843 --> 00:40:36.210
None of them suspects
they ever left their planet.

00:40:36.246 --> 00:40:39.340
However, our success
has come at a high price.

00:40:39.383 --> 00:40:42.682
I think it was some form
of ritual suicide.

00:40:42.719 --> 00:40:45.313
He said that he had
nowhere to go.

00:40:45.355 --> 00:40:49.086
He would have died
even if we hadn't interfered.

00:40:49.126 --> 00:40:51.686
But he wouldn't
have died alone...

00:40:51.728 --> 00:40:53.355
and afraid.

00:40:53.397 --> 00:40:56.525
Are you saying you're sorry
we saved the Boraalans?

00:40:56.567 --> 00:40:57.693
No, of course not.

00:40:57.734 --> 00:41:00.396
Our plan for them
worked out well.

00:41:01.638 --> 00:41:05.699
But I wish that Vorin
could have bridged the gap

00:41:05.742 --> 00:41:07.869
between our two cultures.

00:41:07.911 --> 00:41:12.644
I would have liked the chance
to have known him better.

00:41:26.163 --> 00:41:28.256
What?

00:41:30.634 --> 00:41:32.795
Go inside.

00:41:32.836 --> 00:41:33.894
Nikolai, don't.

00:41:34.004 --> 00:41:35.198
Please.

00:41:51.321 --> 00:41:52.811
I told you

00:41:52.856 --> 00:41:55.757
you would have to kill me
to get me away from here.

00:41:55.792 --> 00:42:00.320
I do not want to fight you,
Nikolai.

00:42:05.102 --> 00:42:08.594
Things were never easy
between us, were they?

00:42:10.907 --> 00:42:12.898
No.

00:42:15.612 --> 00:42:18.740
It's my fault.

00:42:18.782 --> 00:42:22.741
If I had been more like you,
we wouldn't have had

00:42:22.786 --> 00:42:24.981
so many problems.

00:42:25.022 --> 00:42:26.512
No.

00:42:26.556 --> 00:42:29.423
If you had been more like me

00:42:29.459 --> 00:42:32.223
these people
would not be here now.

00:42:35.899 --> 00:42:38.367
You gave them
a chance at a new life.

00:42:38.402 --> 00:42:41.667
And I intend to share
that life with them.

00:42:41.705 --> 00:42:44.697
The village will need
a new Chronicle.

00:42:44.741 --> 00:42:47.039
Someone has to begin it.

00:42:47.077 --> 00:42:49.102
My child will need a father.

00:42:50.747 --> 00:42:53.238
My place is here.

00:42:53.283 --> 00:42:56.184
I'm finally taking
responsibility.

00:43:01.525 --> 00:43:04.289
You were never good at drawing.

00:43:04.327 --> 00:43:06.295
How will you keep a Chronicle?

00:43:06.329 --> 00:43:07.660
I learn quickly.

00:43:07.698 --> 00:43:11.225
Then perhaps there is hope.

00:43:33.924 --> 00:43:36.222
Could I take this with me?

00:43:36.259 --> 00:43:37.351
Hmm...

00:43:37.394 --> 00:43:38.759
It's yours.

00:43:44.768 --> 00:43:46.998
I will have
to explain all of this

00:43:47.037 --> 00:43:48.664
to Mother and Father.

00:43:48.705 --> 00:43:50.468
They won't understand.

00:43:50.507 --> 00:43:52.566
They may.

00:43:52.609 --> 00:43:55.203
I will tell them...

00:43:55.245 --> 00:43:56.872
that you are happy.
